QModem Advance Modem Settings: tables laid out right under Vantage

Three tabs of Advance Modem Settings broke under the Vantage theme, each from a theme rule
written for LuCI's own tables:

- Lock Band: Vantage gives every .td height: 44px. In a table cell that is a minimum, but the
  band list cell and the button rows (createBtnRow, patch 0011) are display: flex, where it is
  a fixed height. The second line of bands ran under Select All / Submit, the last band (n79)
  hung out of the card, and the buttons ran over the card's bottom edge (Dial Mode's Submit
  too). Both get height: auto; the band cell gets a class (qm-band-cell) to be picked by.
- Dial Mode: Vantage makes div.left display: block. The Current Mode and Dial Mode cells are
  div.td.left, so they left the table and stacked, out of line with their titles. Cells of
  the page's tables stay table cells.
- Neighbor Cell (patch 0012): Vantage sticks table titles below its top bar. The cell table
  sits in a horizontal scroller, so the titles stuck to the scroller instead, pushed down by
  the top bar's height over the first row, and the serving (Connected) cell was hidden. The
  titles of that table do not stick, as Vantage already does for LuCI's own tables in a
  scroller.

Applies to: https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git @ 0988085b, after 0014.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

--- a/luci/luci-app-qmodem/luasrc/view/qmodem/modem_debug.htm
+++ b/luci/luci-app-qmodem/luasrc/view/qmodem/modem_debug.htm
@@ -481,6 +481,7 @@
 					td = document.createElement('td');
 					td.classList.add("cbi-section-table-cell");
 					td.classList.add("td")
+					td.classList.add("qm-band-cell");
 					td.style.display = "flex";
 					td.style.flexWrap = "wrap";
 					//clear tr
@@ -2130,6 +2131,29 @@
 	.qm-nc-guard { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
 	.qm-nc-guard > .qm-nc-minutes { width: 5em; min-width: 0; }
 	.qm-nc-check > input[type="checkbox"] + span { margin: 0; }
+
+	/* CleanWRT: three Vantage rules that break this page's tables.
+	   - Every .td is height: 44px. In a table cell that is a minimum, but the band
+	     list and the button rows are display: flex, where it is a fixed height: the
+	     second line of bands ran over Select All / Submit, the last band out of the
+	     card, and the buttons over the card's bottom edge.
+	   - div.left is display: block, so Dial Mode's div.td.left cells left the table
+	     and stacked under each other, out of line with their titles.
+	   - A table title sticks below the top bar, but inside a horizontal scroller it
+	     sticks to the scroller instead, pushed down over the first row: the Neighbor
+	     Cell table hid the serving (Connected) cell under its titles. */
+	td.qm-btn-row,
+	td.qm-band-cell {
+		height: auto;
+	}
+
+	.cbi-section-table div.td.left {
